<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Idalion</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 BCE – 450 BCE (approx.) · capital Idalion</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Inland Cypriot kingdom famous for the Idalion Tablet, a bronze contract recording how the city paid a doctor to treat the wounded during a siege.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Idalion grew on the hills of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a>-bearing foothills of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troodos-mountains">Troodos</a>, in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>. By the 7th century BCE it was a city-kingdom listed among Cypriot states paying tribute to the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a>. Its acropolis held sanctuaries of the goddesses later called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a> and Aphrodite.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Idalion controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> production and fertile land. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idalion-tablet">Idalion Tablet</a>, a bronze plaque of the early 5th century BCE written in the Cypriot syllabary, records that King Stasicypros and the city granted land to the physician Onasilos and his brothers for treating those wounded when 'the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> and the Kitians' besieged the town.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Idalion was conquered by the Phoenician <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kition">Kingdom of Kition</a> c. 450 BCE and lost its independence, Kition then ruling it with Phoenician administration. The town continued under Ptolemaic and Roman rule but declined.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1000 BCE – 450 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:39.80%;width:10.95%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 BCE – 450 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Idalion</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stasicypros</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Cypriot Greek religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arcado-Cypriot Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Cyprus</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Idalion, Idalium</dd></dl></aside></div>

